# Scenario 'mail_receive_var': おくる/うけとる with eleven mails of unusual shape on the fake POP3 server (traces/net/mail_*.eml, tools/trace/make_fixtures.py): headers folded
# over several lines and encoded words split across them, upper-case header names and an upper-case encoded-word prefix, a Q-encoded word and a
# quoted-printable body, a header containing a byte >= 0x80, two mails whose X-Game-code is not the Trainer's (CGB-AAAA-00 is in the ROM's allow-list
# 0F:4004, CGB-ZZZZ-99 is not), a three-part multipart message (text + two base64 parts, one with a name) and a multipart message without its closing
# boundary. The ROM's answer per mail (accepted, refused, "game code" dialogs, limit dialog) is whatever the screens show; the receive loop runs to the end.
# Round 1 used six mails. Starts from the state left by 'mail_send' (empty mailbox). Screen names = my reading of the screenshots.
wait 400                     # boot
waitstable 60 max 600
gap 30
tap A                        # title "スタート"
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # top menu: メール
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # おくる/うけとる
waitstable 60 max 300
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # はい
waitstable 60 max 600
tap A                        # "0でつうしんをはじめる"
waitstable 60 max 300
wait 1500
shot receiving_1
wait 2500
shot receiving_2
wait 2500
shot receiving_3
waitstable 120 max 8000
shot comm_finished
tap A                        # dismiss
waitstable 60 max 600
shot result_1
tap A
waitstable 60 max 600
shot result_2
tap A                        # mailbox list opens
waitstable 60 max 600
shot list
tap DOWN x3
wait 100
shot list_down_3
tap DOWN x3
wait 100
shot list_down_6
tap DOWN x3
wait 100
shot list_down_9
